cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "ChIPBindVis: ChIP-seq Signal and Peak Visualization at Gene Promoters"
abstract: >-
  ChIPBindVis is an R package for visualizing ChIP-seq signal and called
  peaks around a selected gene and across genes with promoter-associated
  peaks. It produces a Gviz track centered on the selected gene's TSS and a
  strand-aware EnrichedHeatmap across gene-level TSSs. The query gene is
  highlighted only when a promoter-associated peak is detected within the
  configured annotation window. It supports human (hg38, hg19) and mouse
  (mm10, mm39) reference assemblies.
